  1. Go by the Azores: land in sight, about 4 days longer, and a risk  [The autopilot takes her 30 km south of Pico, under its 2,351 m mountain, then on to the same finish line. Most of our test crossings took 1 to 7 days longer than the autopilot's own route, and the worst 10, so the ghost will pull ahead. Islands mean fishing boats and their gear: about 1 crossing in 10 that would have finished did not, most of them taken or snagged within 150 km of the islands.]
  2. Stay on the autopilot's route (same as the ghost)  [No land until Portugal, and no days lost]
